## 2. Licence grant

Subject to your compliance with this agreement and receipt of payment in full,
Licensor grants You a perpetual, worldwide, non-exclusive, non-transferable,
non-sublicensable licence to:

1. use, copy, and modify the Template for the purpose of producing Generated
   Applications, within the scope of your purchased tier (Section 3);
2. use, modify, deploy, distribute, sell, and otherwise commercially exploit
   Generated Applications without restriction and without payment of any
   further fee; and
3. permit Developers within your organisation to access the Template for those
   purposes.

The licence is perpetual: it does not expire and is not contingent on any
ongoing subscription or renewal.

---

## 3. Licence tiers

Your tier is the one identified on your purchase receipt.

### 3.1 Single Application

Permits use of the Template to produce **one** Generated Application. The
application may be developed, deployed, and maintained without limit as to
time, environments, servers, or end users, and may be built for a client.

Producing a second, unrelated application requires an additional licence.
Re-generating, rewriting, or rebuilding the *same* application does not.

### 3.2 Unlimited Applications

Permits use of the Template to produce an **unlimited** number of Generated
Applications, including applications built for clients or employers.

### 3.3 Developer access

Both tiers permit access by Developers within a single organisation. Access by
a separate legal entity — a contractor's own firm, a subsidiary operating
independently, or a partner company — requires that entity to hold its own
licence, unless they are working on your Generated Application under your
direction and do not retain the Template afterwards.

