## 4. Restrictions

You may **not**:

1. sell, resell, rent, lease, sublicense, distribute, or otherwise make the
   Template available to any third party, whether modified or unmodified,
   except as expressly permitted in Section 3.3;
2. publish the Template, or any substantial portion of it, to any public or
   shared repository, package registry, forum, file host, dataset, or other
   location from which third parties may obtain it;
3. share your purchase credentials, download links, or repository access with
   anyone outside your organisation;
4. use the Template, in whole or in substantial part, to create or contribute
   to any product that competes with it — including any application template,
   boilerplate, starter kit, scaffolding generator, or code-generation product
   or service intended for distribution to third parties;
5. use the Template, in whole or in substantial part, as training data for any
   machine learning model that is distributed to or made available to third
   parties; or
6. remove, obscure, or alter any copyright, licence, or attribution notice
   contained in the Template.

For the avoidance of doubt: Section 4 restricts distribution of the **Template**.
It places no restriction whatsoever on your Generated Applications.

